  "reason": "The largest performance jump in the history (0.537→0.725) came from switching to multiprofile, but we cannot yet tell how much of that gain is driven by the multiprofile aggregation itself versus the multimodal combination. config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) is a clean single-factor ablation of the image modality from the current best config_043. If RNA-only multiprofile approaches ~0.70, the image adds little and future effort should target RNA encoders (e.g., scgpt). If it drops substantially (e.g., below 0.60), the image is essential and we should explore image-encoder variants (resnet50) and fusion strategies. This single experiment resolves a major design uncertainty that will determine the direction of all subsequent experiments, making it the highest-information-use choice under the limited budget."
}

